u_{\mu}$ transition, within the framework of Heavy Quark Effective Theory and Standard Model predictions, while also incorporating existing $bightarrow s$ differential decay rate data. Our results are available on the LHCb LHCb-ENTAs data platform, enabling LHCb experimenters to compare their future differential decay rate measurements with theoretical predictions. Additionally, we discuss potential ANcock corrections for the distribution, which we cast in a form suitable for $R$-ratio definitions. This suitable form is also available on the LHCb-ENTAs data platform. The input parameters used are taken from the 2019 world average values. The assessment for the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ differential decay rate is also applicable to the $B_d^0ightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ transition, which is a near identity transformation of the former. The assessment conditions are further used to combine the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ and $B_d^0ightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ differential decay rate predictions for ASyCut functions at three-momentum values of 10 GeV, following the instructions provided in the Euroworkshop on the hadronization of heavy quarks in 2001. The combined assessment for the $B_d^0ightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
